course: dictionary
lesson: 8535
title: Sawdust
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sawdust is the tiny bits of wood that fall off when you cut wood with a saw. The word is two words joined together: saw and dust. Dust is very fine powder, so sawdust is powder made by sawing.
explain: Use the context to work out the meaning. «Carpenter bees chew tunnels in wood for their nests and push the sawdust out instead of eating it.» Bees chew wood, so what they push out must be small pieces of wood. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Sawdust can also stand for something very small. «Why do you look at the speck of sawdust in your brother's eye and pay no attention to the plank in your own eye?» A speck is tiny, and a plank is a big board. The question compares a small fault in someone else with a big fault in yourself.
fact: Sawdust is uncountable, so you say some sawdust or a pile of sawdust, not a sawdust.
fact: «Sawdust» means tiny pieces of wood that fall off when wood is cut with a saw.
fact: Sawdust is used as bedding for hamsters and guinea pigs, to soak up spills, and to make chipboard.
fact: Sawdust burns easily, so it is a fire risk; when sawing wood, wear goggles and a mask.
fact: Two useful phrases are «covered in sawdust» and «a pile of sawdust».
exercise: «Carpenter bees push the sawdust out of their tunnels.» What is sawdust? | Wet mud from the garden | *Tiny pieces of wood cut off by a saw | Soft leaves that fall from trees | A type of bee
exercise: Hamsters sleep on sawdust bedding. Why might a pet owner use sawdust? | It is a food that hamsters love most | *It is soft and soaks up mess | It keeps the hamster dry in the rain | It makes the hamster fly
exercise: «The workshop floor was covered in sawdust after the carpenter cut the planks.» What does covered in sawdust mean? | Painted all over in bright colours | *Lots of tiny bits of wood on the floor | Very wet from the rain | Hidden under a big blanket
test: Why must you be careful with sawdust near a fire? | Sawdust turns into ice | *Sawdust burns easily and can start a fire | Sawdust is too heavy to lift | Sawdust is slippery and makes you fall
test: In «the speck of sawdust in your eye», which thing is the smallest? | The eye | *The speck of sawdust | The brother | The plank
exam: Which sentence uses sawdust correctly? | *The carpenter swept up the sawdust from the floor | The sawdust is a great big tree | Sawdust is a bird that flies high | The sawdust was very loud and fast
